Vaulta migrations

Fresh database:      alembic upgrade head      (from the repo root, DATABASE_URL set)
New migration:       alembic revision -m "..."  — import any new model in env.py

History starts at 0b5e1a9c7d21 (baseline: the users table that predates
Alembic), then 45e4169519ab (phase1_initial) onwards.

Existing databases (Neon) were created before the baseline existed. Their
alembic_version holds a revision at or after 45e4169519ab, which descends
from the baseline, so Alembic treats the baseline as applied and `alembic
upgrade head` just continues from where they are. No stamping is needed.
Only a database whose schema exists but whose alembic_version table is
missing needs `alembic stamp 45e4169519ab` (or the revision its schema
matches) before upgrading.

backend/tests/test_migrations.py builds a fresh database, upgrades,
downgrades to base, upgrades again and checks the result matches the models.
